        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>The Stonewyrm exhales a poisonus gas that turns flesh to stone. </p><p>Creatures in an @Template[cone|distance:80] take @Damage[11d6[poison]|options:area-damage] (@Check[fortitude|dc:32|basic|options:area-effect] save) with the following additional effects. </p><p>The Stonewyrm can't use this ability again for [[/gmr 1d4 #Recharge Poisonous Exhalation]]{1d4 rounds}.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} and @UUID[Compendium.covalon.whitespire-items.Item.dW8603EhXd6F1tgY]{Turning to Stone}.</p><p>The target must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:29] save at the end of each of its turns. On a failed save, the slowed condition increases by 1 (or 2 on a critical failure). A successful save reduces the slowed condition by 1.</p><p>If a creature becomes fully unable to act due to the slowed condition, they become petrified permanently as a stone statue.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, and then as Failure, except it is initially @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 2}.</p>"
        },
