      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
      "name": "Raise Cliffs",
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "sort": 0,
      "system": {
        "_migration": {
          "previous": {
            "foundry": "13.351",
            "schema": null,
            "system": "7.10.1"
          },
          "version": 0.955
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "action"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": 1
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>The Stonewyrm raises up to three @UUID[Compendium.covalon.whitespire-actors.Actor.1S5SJtiUINUpn3wy]{Raise Cliffs Wall (T4)} from the earth anywhere in the arena. Each wall is 1 inch thick, 30 feet long, and reaches from the floor to the ceiling (60 ft up).</p><p>Walls are placed on the border between squares, must be conjured in an open space in a straight line, and cannot pass through creatures or objects. You cannot form a closed triangle with this ability (you can make three walls of a box). When placed in parallel, each wall must be at least 10 feet apart.</p><p>You can use the drawing tool or a @Template[line|distance:30|width:0.25] template to mark the location of each wall. Track each wall's HP using a separate @UUID[Compendium.covalon.whitespire-actors.Actor.1S5SJtiUINUpn3wy]{Raise Cliffs Wall (T4)} actor.</p><p>Walls automatically fail their saving throws. When a wall is destroyed, it destroys the entire 30 foot segment.</p><div data-visibility=\"gm\"><p>If using the Obsidian Spikes modification: when a wall takes damage from a creature within 10 feet, it deals piercing damage back. See @UUID[Compendium.covalon.whitespire-actors.Actor.1S5SJtiUINUpn3wy.Item.ptZqTGRQ5BH0i7VM]{Modification: Obsidian Spikes}.</p></div><p>If the Stonewyrm uses this ability again, any previous walls disappear.</p>"
        },
